Description: reliable PostgreSQL backup and restore (continuity fork of pgBackRest)
 pgxbackup is a backup and restore solution for PostgreSQL that scales to the
 largest databases and workloads. It is a continuity fork of pgBackRest,
 maintained by pgExperts after the upstream project was declared end-of-life
 in early 2026.
 .
 Features include parallel backup and restore, full/differential/incremental
 backups (file or block level), per-file checksums, page checksums validated
 during backup, multiple compression types, encryption, partial-failed backup
 resume, backup from standby, tablespace and link support, S3/Azure/GCS/SFTP
 repositories, archive expiration, and local or remote operation via SSH or
 TLS.
 .
 The on-disk repository format is fully compatible with upstream pgBackRest
 (versions through 2.58); existing backups can be restored by either tool, and
 the legacy /etc/pgbackrest.conf is read by pgxbackup out of the box. The
 pgxbackup package coexists with the pgbackrest package -- both can be
 installed during a migration.
